invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: read_psk_binders admits a PskBinderEntry under 32 bytes, which RFC
  9846 §4.2.11 bounds at <32..255> because the shortest binder is one
  SHA-256 HMAC. A shorter entry cannot carry one, so the binder check the
  PSK lane adds would compare against bytes that are not there.
  test/srv_parser_tests.h sends 15- and 16-byte entries that fill the
  binders list exactly, so no later check refuses them first.

--- old
        if (rb_bytes(e, binder_len) == NULL || binder_len < PSK_BINDER_MIN) {
--- new
        if (rb_bytes(e, binder_len) == NULL) {
